   B1: L = r x v exact for central fields under scalar dressing (any memory);
   B2: E(t) = v^2/2 - INT (v.g_bar)/mu dt' = const (the exact energy-balance functional);
   B3: two-body dressed momentum P(t) - M g_ext t = const; bare CoM wander MEASURED and
       matched to its analytic third-law defect integral.
   B1 angular momentum:   max |L/L0 - 1|            = 6.100e-11
   B2 energy functional:  max |E(t)-E(0)|/(v0^2/2)  = 1.815e-10
   [PASS] B1 L conserved to < 1e-8 (exact law; residual = integrator error)
   [PASS] B2 energy-balance functional conserved to < 1e-8
   B3 dressed momentum:   max |P(t)-P(0)|/M v_rel   = 4.963e-18
      bare momentum:      max |sum m v - const|/Mv  = 5.430e-02   <- PHYSICAL (MI third-law)
   [PASS] B3a dressed momentum functional conserved to < 1e-9 (the action's own balance law)
      defect-integral consistency: |dP_bare - INT defect dt| / max|dP_bare| = 2.767e-05
   [PASS] B3b bare-momentum wander is REAL (> 1e-3) and EQUALS the analytic third-law defect integral to < 1% (the wander is the theory's physics, not integrator error)
      CoM excursion growth (the per-orbit defect kick has a nonzero mean along the
      apsis line of the slightly eccentric orbit; the apsis precesses slowly):
        periods =  4: max CoM excursion = 0.4250 r12
        periods = 16: max CoM excursion = 1.7176 r12
        periods = 64: max CoM excursion = 7.0280 r12
      growth exponent (4 -> 64 periods): 1.01  (1 = ballistic drift, 0 = bounded)
      => the drift is BALLISTIC over the run horizon: V_com ~ 9.56 m/s (= 1.75% of v_rel), constant, direction set by the slowly precessing apsis.
      This is the instrument MEASURING the theory's third-law violation (its size is
      the defect integral, B3b): the published action's own conserved object is the DRESSED
      momentum (B3a, machine-exact); the bare CoM self-drift is real, secular on the run
      horizon, and quoted straight -- a falsifiable N-body signature of scalar per-star MI
      dressing, not an integrator artifact (B3b pins it to the analytic defect).
   [PASS] B3c the bare-CoM drift is characterized: ballistic exponent in [0.8, 1.2] over 4 -> 64 periods, rate quoted, and identified with the defect integral (B3b)

